  "name": "Lehakot tzva'iyot (Israeli army entertainment troupes)",
  "family": "pop",
  "lineage": "Entertainment troupes of the Israel Defense Forces, beginning with the Nahal troupe founded in 1950 and followed by the Central Command, Northern Command, Navy and other unit troupes, in which conscript singers performed songs, sketches and choreographed numbers for soldiers and civilian audiences. Songwriters including Naomi Shemer and Yair Rosenblum wrote for them, their LPs on Hed Arzi and CBS Israel carried the songs to radio from the 1950s to the 1970s, and many Israeli popular singers began their careers in them.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1950s lehakot tzva'iyot, functional Song, pop rock branch. accordion, acoustic guitar, upright piano, upright bass, machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows full lathed both sides lathed drum kit. treated studio. Telefunken ELA M 251, tube pre, German tube console, vari-mu, Pultec passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
